<title>HONG KONG: HK to tender 5-year 6.57 pct govt notes on Dec 16.</title>
<headline>HK to tender 5-year 6.57 pct govt notes on Dec 16.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong Monetary Authority (HKMA) said on Monday it will tender its 10th issue of five-year Exchange Fund notes on December 16.</p>
<p>The HK$500 million notes carry a coupon of 6.57 percent per annum, with interest payable semi-annually in arrears.</p>
<p>The notes will mature on December 17, 2001.</p>
<p>An additional HK$100 million will be held as reserve by the HKMA for supply to market makers in the secondary market.</p>
<p>Settlement will take place on December 17, 2001, the HKMA said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
